Z||000000||Bluemagic||05-02-2001||08:46 AM||||Ijust bought a 120 mph speedo instrument panel for my 85 SE and after installing it I noticed that the water temp needle was missing,you can imagine how I felt but a light was at the end of the tunnel try the forum if they can't help then no one can.If any one has a non functioning gauge that has a water temp needle or a gauge and want to sell it let me know .||||reg||8
Z||000001||rogergarrison||05-02-2001||10:44 AM||||all the needles just press onto the shaft. Im pretty sure all the gages, amp, oil, temp, fuel are the same. just get a good grip on it and pull. some are pretty stubborn. just make sure you pull it straight so you dont bend the tiny shaft. new one just pushes on. not hard, just enough to keep it on. Speedo and tach needles are the same too I think. Your original needle is probably in the cluster somewhere. I know Lisas temp gage fell off too, was laying in the bottom of gauge under the clear cover.||||reg||1
